{"id":"s4.1.5","slug":"multiplying-by-fraction-close-to-1","title":"Multiplying by Fraction Close to 1","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">This trick involves clever factoring when multiplying a whole number by a fraction close to 1. By treating the fraction as $(1 \\pm \\text{small fraction})$, you can simplify the calculation.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">For $14 \\times \\frac{15}{16}$, rewrite it as $14 \\times (1 - \\frac{1}{16}) = 14 - \\frac{14}{16} = 13\\frac{1}{8}$.</p><p>For $17 \\times \\frac{13}{11}$, rewrite it as $17 \\times (1 + \\frac{2}{11}) = 17 + \\frac{34}{11} = 17 + 3\\frac{1}{11} = 20\\frac{1}{11}$. This avoids dealing with large improper fractions.</p>","summary":"This trick involves clever factoring when multiplying a whole number by a fraction close to 1.","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem multiplying a whole number by a fraction very close to 1.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $6 \\times \\frac{7}{8} + 5$. (mixed number)","answer":"10 1/4","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $13 \\times \\frac{14}{15}$. (mixed number)","answer":"12 2/15","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $18 \\times \\frac{19}{20}$. (mixed number)","answer":"17 1/10","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $12 \\times \\frac{13}{14}$. (mixed number)","answer":"11 1/7","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $13 \\times \\frac{13}{14} + 13$. (mixed number)","answer":"25 1/14","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $11 \\times \\frac{12}{13}$. (mixed number)","answer":"10 2/13","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate $11 \\times \\frac{14}{17}$. (mixed number)","answer":"9 1/17","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed